WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:09.031
[theme music playing]

3
00:46.694 --> 00:50.656
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

4
00:50.781 --> 00:52.491
[theme music concludes]

5
00:52.616 --> 00:53.492
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS, INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

6
00:53.617 --> 00:54.451
ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:54.577 --> 00:55.411
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

8
00:55.536 --> 00:56.370
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

9
00:57.079 --> 00:58.038
[mid-tempo music playing]

10
00:59.790 --> 01:02.001
-[young Yeong-do] Mom! It's spicy! -[young Ms. Ma] Okay, okay, here.

11
01:02.126 --> 01:05.004
-Here, have some water. Here. -[young Yeong-do] Water! [groans]

12
01:05.754 --> 01:07.798
I'll finish eating in a minute, okay? I'll watch Wan-do.

13
01:07.923 --> 01:08.757
It's fine.

14
01:08.883 --> 01:09.842
You'll get a stomachache.

15
01:09.967 --> 01:10.801
Take your time.

16
01:10.926 --> 01:12.177
Oh, no.

17
01:12.636 --> 01:13.888
When did this spill, huh?

18
01:14.013 --> 01:15.431
-I just bought you these clothes. -Hmm?

19
01:15.556 --> 01:17.725
[young Ms. Ma] Let's keep them clean, okay?

20
01:17.850 --> 01:18.893
[sighs]

21
01:19.852 --> 01:20.895
Hmm, eat.

22
01:21.020 --> 01:21.937
[groans]

23
01:22.855 --> 01:24.315
So you won't eat, huh?

24
01:25.399 --> 01:27.067
Well, is the kimchi not good?

25
01:27.192 --> 01:28.027
Spicy?

26
01:28.611 --> 01:29.445
Papa!

27
01:29.904 --> 01:32.573
Tell her that I'm not a baby who can't eat kimchi.

28
01:33.657 --> 01:34.909
Hmm.

29
01:35.659 --> 01:36.577
Lee Mi-do.

30
01:37.036 --> 01:38.203
This going to continue, huh?

31
01:39.204 --> 01:41.248
It's been two weeks already.

32
01:41.373 --> 01:44.168
And if you're so mad at me, just tell me straight.

33
01:44.293 --> 01:46.211
[Mi-do's father] Hmm, I'll talk to her.

34
01:46.337 --> 01:47.546
Jeez, this girl.

35
01:49.632 --> 01:51.050
What's wrong with my princess, huh?

36
01:51.926 --> 01:54.219
I get sad when you're like this on a family trip.

37
01:55.095 --> 01:56.096
What is it?

38
01:56.221 --> 01:57.264
It's because of piano class.

39
01:58.265 --> 02:01.101
Okay, I'll start saving up my extra pay this month.

40
02:01.685 --> 02:02.519
Hmm?

41
02:03.145 --> 02:05.064
Oh, it's not that? Then what?

42
02:05.189 --> 02:06.023
Art class?

43
02:06.398 --> 02:07.858
Ballet class? Hmm?

44
02:07.983 --> 02:10.277
[young Yeong-do] Oh! I want to do taekwondo!

45
02:10.402 --> 02:12.154
-[young Ms. Ma] Oh! -Taekwondo! [laughs]

46
02:12.279 --> 02:13.322
I hear ya!

47
02:13.447 --> 02:15.407
-[young Ms. Ma laughs] -I want a fire truck!

48
02:15.532 --> 02:16.909
[young Ms. Ma] A fire truck? Oh!

49
02:17.034 --> 02:18.118
I want something too!

50
02:18.243 --> 02:19.244
Please buy me a lipstick.

51
02:19.370 --> 02:20.871
-[Mi-do's father] A lipstick? -[young Ms. Ma] Yes!

52
02:20.996 --> 02:22.706
[Mi-do's father] A lipstick for my lovely wife.

53
02:22.831 --> 02:24.249
[laughs]

54
02:24.375 --> 02:28.379
My life's been totally messed up since I met your ma. [sighs]

55
02:28.504 --> 02:31.423
-[Mi-do's family chatting happily] -[mid-tempo music concludes]

56
02:33.008 --> 02:34.301
[Mr. Jeong exhales wearily]

57
02:34.426 --> 02:35.636
It's messed up.

58
02:36.637 --> 02:39.390
After everything I've done for her. Hmm?

59
02:40.099 --> 02:41.100
[scoffs]

60
02:41.225 --> 02:44.561
I even raised her brat who doesn't share a drop of my blood.

61
02:45.479 --> 02:46.313
Shit.

62
02:49.984 --> 02:50.818
What?

63
02:52.236 --> 02:54.029
You don't like that I'm insulting your Ma?

64
02:54.154 --> 02:55.322
I know that Mom

65
02:55.864 --> 02:58.867
and that hardware store guy have nothing going on.

66
02:58.993 --> 02:59.910
You think?

67
03:00.035 --> 03:04.081
He had to come to our house today to fix a broken light.

68
03:04.665 --> 03:06.125
He just came to fix it.

69
03:06.375 --> 03:07.710
[scoffs]

70
03:09.586 --> 03:14.842
You know, too? You know that your ma isn't coming back for you.

71
03:19.596 --> 03:22.891
Well, I guess we're in this together.

72
03:23.726 --> 03:24.643
[huffs]

73
03:25.269 --> 03:26.353
[Mi-do's father] All right, let's go.

74
03:26.478 --> 03:27.604
[young Yeong-do] I'm first, Dad!

75
03:27.730 --> 03:29.148
[young Ms. Ma] Slow down, slow down.

76
03:31.483 --> 03:32.693
-[clatters] -[young Namgung yelps]

77
03:32.818 --> 03:35.070
[server] Oh no, I'm sorry. Are you okay?

78
03:35.195 --> 03:36.196
Mi-do!

79
03:36.321 --> 03:38.282
[server] I'm very sorry, sir. Are you okay?

80
03:40.784 --> 03:42.786
-[soft music playing] -[server] Does it burn?

81
03:43.996 --> 03:45.289
He must be scared.

82
03:46.707 --> 03:48.375
Again, I'm so incredibly sorry.

83
03:48.500 --> 03:49.626
[Mr. Jeong] Don't worry.

84
03:49.752 --> 03:50.586
It's okay.

85
03:51.545 --> 03:53.422
[young Ms. Ma] You should really take him to a doctor.

86
03:53.547 --> 03:54.715
I'll take care of him.

87
03:54.840 --> 03:56.133
[young Ms. Ma] You want us to…

88
03:56.759 --> 03:59.636
She looks like Kim Hee-sun, your mother.

89
04:02.097 --> 04:03.223
Do you like dinosaurs?

90
04:05.517 --> 04:08.312
No, you fell for it because my mom did that for you.

91
04:08.645 --> 04:09.855
But it doesn't do anything.

92
04:10.481 --> 04:12.232
My mom is stronger than a dinosaur, you know?

93
04:12.608 --> 04:14.568
Have you ever been hit in the head with a handbag?

94
04:15.319 --> 04:16.236
It's very painful.

95
04:16.361 --> 04:18.363
[laughs] That is not painful.

96
04:19.698 --> 04:21.116
[Mi-do's father] Just please give me your word.

97
04:21.867 --> 04:23.118
Take him to a doctor now.

98
04:23.243 --> 04:24.244
Then call us, please.

99
04:24.369 --> 04:25.579
I've memorized your pager number.

100
04:25.704 --> 04:26.830
Hey, hey, stop.

101
04:26.955 --> 04:28.707
You keep saying the same thing.

102
04:28.832 --> 04:30.375
[young Yeong-do] Left, right. Yeah!

103
04:30.501 --> 04:31.376
Hey.

104
04:34.171 --> 04:37.257
Sweetie, you must be scared.

105
04:37.382 --> 04:38.801
I'm very sorry.

106
04:42.805 --> 04:43.889
Go to a doctor, please.

107
04:44.765 --> 04:45.599
Will you go?

108
04:45.974 --> 04:46.809
Swear?

109
04:48.685 --> 04:50.604
Hurry, I don't have all day.

110
04:58.112 --> 04:58.987
Hey!

111
05:03.909 --> 05:05.369
Since you seem to like dinosaurs.

112
05:15.587 --> 05:17.589
[Mr. Jeong] What are you waiting for? Come on.

113
05:24.805 --> 05:26.056
[waves crashing gently]

114
05:26.598 --> 05:28.058
[young Ms. Ma] I hope he saw a doctor.

115
05:30.018 --> 05:32.521
[sighs] I think we should have gone with them.

116
05:32.646 --> 05:33.856
[soft music concludes]

117
05:34.398 --> 05:35.524
He gave me his pager number.

118
05:36.984 --> 05:38.902
And he says he knows the restaurant owner,

119
05:39.027 --> 05:42.406
so if he doesn't call by tonight, we'll ask.

120
05:43.532 --> 05:44.533
Hmm…

121
05:48.287 --> 05:51.123
Then again, I have my own things to worry about.

122
05:54.376 --> 05:55.752
Well, what is it now?

123
05:56.670 --> 05:58.463
Is this about the cotton candy?

124
05:58.589 --> 05:59.965
You can have some too.

125
06:00.591 --> 06:02.676
I didn't just buy it for your brother, all right?

126
06:03.218 --> 06:06.430
Papa, can you tell her that I hate having cotton candy

127
06:06.555 --> 06:07.723
because it rots your teeth?

128
06:07.848 --> 06:09.183
[laughs]

129
06:11.185 --> 06:14.146
Papa, could you ask her why she's sulking so much?

130
06:14.479 --> 06:17.691
And besides, she's acting like a total baby right now.

131
06:17.816 --> 06:19.693
Honey, what is it you're doing?

132
06:22.112 --> 06:24.448
Can my princess whisper the answer just to me?

133
06:25.490 --> 06:26.700
What made you so upset?

134
06:28.076 --> 06:29.494
Oh, just leave her alone.

135
06:29.953 --> 06:32.748
You keep doing that and you're just spoiling her.

136
06:32.873 --> 06:36.126
Oh, plus she never listens and always causes trouble.

137
06:36.251 --> 06:37.252
I'm done with it.

138
06:37.711 --> 06:40.047
I should just abandon her at some random house.

139
06:40.547 --> 06:42.549
When you get old, I'm going to abandon you.

140
06:43.258 --> 06:45.427
I'll leave you deep in the mountains all alone!

141
06:49.806 --> 06:51.433
[somber music playing]

142
06:58.148 --> 06:59.149
What did you say?

143
07:00.984 --> 07:02.027
Lee Mi-do.

144
07:02.986 --> 07:04.738
I learned it in history class.

145
07:05.405 --> 07:06.323
It's goryeojang.

146
07:06.448 --> 07:09.326
When parents got old, they left them alone in the woods.

147
07:10.244 --> 07:12.120
My teacher taught me all that, Dad.

148
07:12.246 --> 07:13.205
That's wrong.

149
07:13.789 --> 07:15.624
It's bad, and you should never do that.

150
07:16.416 --> 07:17.668
That's what your teacher told you.

151
07:18.252 --> 07:20.629
Listen, Mi-do, you really hurt Mom's feelings now.

152
07:21.046 --> 07:22.673
You said a really mean thing to her.

153
07:22.798 --> 07:25.550
But Mom hurt my feelings even more.

154
07:26.093 --> 07:29.346
She forgets every single thing I tell her, and it happens all the time.

155
07:30.055 --> 07:33.558
She forgot I wanted to wear my rabbit fur vest on Friday.

156
07:34.601 --> 07:37.271
She forgot that I'm good at eating spicy food.

157
07:38.063 --> 07:40.816
And she forgot that I wanted to eat the pink ham.

158
07:41.358 --> 07:42.651
And she… [sobs]

159
07:42.776 --> 07:45.779
She forgot the kind of snacks I like, not cotton candy.

160
07:45.904 --> 07:47.531
She forgot everything.

161
07:47.656 --> 07:49.449
[sobbing]

162
07:51.785 --> 07:52.869
[Mi-do's father] There.

163
07:53.787 --> 07:54.997
My sweet Mi-do.

164
07:55.539 --> 07:57.582
You must have been so angry. Hmm?

165
08:00.377 --> 08:01.211
But Mi-do…

166
08:02.587 --> 08:05.632
But your mom doesn't just forget what you tell her.

167
08:06.091 --> 08:07.968
She always forgets what I say, too.

168
08:08.635 --> 08:10.846
I was wearing mismatched socks the other day, remember?

169
08:11.638 --> 08:12.556
Hmm?

170
08:13.473 --> 08:14.891
You will only have one mother.

171
08:15.851 --> 08:17.102
But Mom has three kids.

172
08:17.436 --> 08:19.354
Oh, wait. Four, including me.

173
08:19.813 --> 08:21.398
[music softens]

174
08:21.815 --> 08:23.525
-[Mi-do's father] Mi-do. -[sniffles]

175
08:23.900 --> 08:25.152
You have to tell us, love.

176
08:25.610 --> 08:29.531
If you don't speak up, even though Mom and I love you with all our heart,

177
08:29.990 --> 08:31.408
we cannot read your mind.

178
08:32.743 --> 08:34.870
And it's not because we love you any less.

179
08:36.413 --> 08:39.333
We don't know what's happening to you because you don't tell us.

180
08:41.293 --> 08:45.922
I'd love you to be someone who can be honest about your feelings

181
08:46.048 --> 08:48.842
with the people that are close to you and who love you.

182
08:51.219 --> 08:52.054
Can you do that?

183
08:54.431 --> 08:55.557
Okay, promise.

184
09:00.604 --> 09:01.938
[music concludes]

185
09:06.276 --> 09:07.736
[woman 1] Someone fell in the water!

186
09:07.861 --> 09:08.987
[man] Someone fall in the water!

187
09:09.112 --> 09:10.739
[woman 1] Hurry! We need some help!

188
09:14.284 --> 09:17.079
[crowd gasping]

189
09:17.204 --> 09:18.789
[melancholic music playing]

190
09:20.540 --> 09:23.377
[crowd whispering indistinctly]

191
09:23.502 --> 09:24.544
[woman 2] Such a shame.

192
09:24.961 --> 09:26.129
[woman 3] Such a tragedy.

193
09:28.632 --> 09:31.551
[young Ms. Ma screaming]

194
09:31.676 --> 09:33.720
[sobbing]

195
09:33.845 --> 09:35.806
Come on. Breathe.

196
09:37.474 --> 09:38.600
[wails]

197
09:38.725 --> 09:39.601
Wake up!

198
09:39.726 --> 09:40.644
Wake up right now!

199
09:41.520 --> 09:43.313
[sobbing] Wake up!

200
09:43.438 --> 09:44.272
Wake up!

201
09:44.523 --> 09:46.149
Wake up!

202
09:46.274 --> 09:51.696
[screaming]

203
09:54.116 --> 09:55.325
My baby!

204
09:55.784 --> 09:57.452
My baby!

205
09:57.786 --> 10:00.247
[wailing]

206
10:23.520 --> 10:25.147
[music swells]

207
10:27.816 --> 10:31.695
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

208
10:31.820 --> 10:36.408
WHAT DO OUR SCARS LOOK LIKE?

209
10:36.575 --> 10:37.701
[melancholic music concludes]

210
10:41.788 --> 10:43.915
I will have to reject this estimate.

211
10:45.625 --> 10:47.627
But why? You need to give me a reason.

212
10:48.003 --> 10:49.379
We clearly followed the guidelines.

213
10:49.504 --> 10:50.714
What seems to be the problem here?

214
10:50.839 --> 10:53.258
Is 600 million won really a feasible amount?

215
10:56.511 --> 10:58.346
The costs listed here were calculated

216
10:59.097 --> 11:00.515
to reflect the market price decline

217
11:00.640 --> 11:03.351
resulting from increased raw material procurement.

218
11:03.477 --> 11:07.439
But you completely left out the burden of rising fuel costs on logistics.

219
11:09.441 --> 11:11.985
Surcharges were added due to Middle East oil price risks.

220
11:12.110 --> 11:13.612
You can't submit estimates like this.

221
11:14.571 --> 11:17.949
Either you're incompetent, or this is a deception.

222
11:19.034 --> 11:20.744
I can't just keep this on my end.

223
11:20.869 --> 11:22.746
I will have to report it to the audit team.

224
11:23.705 --> 11:25.499
Submitting a false estimate will be punished.

225
11:26.041 --> 11:28.543
Resubmit it using the last three months' statistics.

226
11:29.044 --> 11:30.795
I'll withhold my approval, gentlemen.

227
11:33.715 --> 11:35.550
[jaunty music playing]

228
11:37.636 --> 11:38.470
[Ho-sik] Who is it?

229
11:38.929 --> 11:40.597
Who is the one to leak our plan?

230
11:46.603 --> 11:47.729
Look me in the eye.

231
11:48.188 --> 11:51.149
In the last week, did Namgung invite you for a drink?

232
11:52.025 --> 11:52.859
Yes, sir.

233
11:52.984 --> 11:54.861
Did Namgung pay for all the drinks?

234
11:55.612 --> 11:56.446
He did.

235
11:56.988 --> 11:58.532
Although, I didn't say anything.

236
11:58.782 --> 11:59.699
You sure?

237
12:00.242 --> 12:01.701
Did you get drunk that day?

238
12:02.410 --> 12:03.245
I was wasted.

239
12:04.829 --> 12:06.456
Ah! But I…

240
12:06.581 --> 12:07.541
[object clatters]

241
12:07.874 --> 12:11.545
You… You… You've committed treason.

242
12:11.920 --> 12:13.630
You sabotaged us all!

243
12:14.256 --> 12:16.091
You told that snake Namgung.

244
12:18.343 --> 12:20.303
I didn't-- I didn't betray you, sir.

245
12:20.428 --> 12:21.596
[stammers] I didn't do it.

246
12:21.721 --> 12:22.556
Who told him?

247
12:22.973 --> 12:24.015
Ms. Park did it?

248
12:24.599 --> 12:25.433
Hmm?

249
12:25.559 --> 12:28.353
She got top evaluations and last year's best employee award.

250
12:28.478 --> 12:30.105
Do you think it was her?

251
12:30.230 --> 12:31.690
She's not stupid like you.

252
12:31.815 --> 12:32.983
[softly] I think I did.

253
12:33.108 --> 12:34.025
Hear that?

254
12:34.150 --> 12:34.985
She said it.

255
12:36.653 --> 12:37.654
Wait, what?

256
12:37.904 --> 12:39.322
But I wasn't drunk.

257
12:40.615 --> 12:41.992
And I'm not stupid.

258
12:45.036 --> 12:46.162
He tricked me.

259
12:48.248 --> 12:50.292
[Namgung] How did TF Team 3's cost adjustment go?

260
12:50.417 --> 12:51.793
As you know, local supply.

261
12:51.918 --> 12:54.838
imported raw material prices vary based on it.

262
12:55.672 --> 13:00.427
He used the increased crop volume as a basis to bluff a bit. [chuckles]

263
13:01.886 --> 13:02.721
That's a relief.

264
13:06.349 --> 13:08.184
A honey trap.

265
13:11.229 --> 13:12.439
He did trick me.

266
13:15.191 --> 13:16.151
[jaunty music fades]

267
13:16.901 --> 13:18.612
I see now that it was a honey trap,

268
13:18.737 --> 13:21.489
you held my hand to get info out of me.

269
13:21.615 --> 13:23.366
Did you join the company because of me?

270
13:24.075 --> 13:27.162
Procurement's initial offer was ridiculous anyway.

271
13:28.038 --> 13:29.873
Did you date Sun-cheol while you liked me?

272
13:29.998 --> 13:31.124
[scoffs]

273
13:31.249 --> 13:33.627
I heard you and Manager Jeong are close now.

274
13:33.752 --> 13:34.878
What happened there?

275
13:35.587 --> 13:37.756
What's Sun-cheol doing lately?

276
13:42.093 --> 13:45.138
You're embarrassing me because you plan to dodge the question.

277
13:45.263 --> 13:46.973
Now, give me a straight answer, please.

278
13:48.975 --> 13:50.352
I follow the rules, Su-a.

279
13:51.978 --> 13:54.230
Procurement can't approve false invoices, right?

280
13:55.398 --> 13:56.232
Agreed?

281
13:58.526 --> 13:59.361
Yeah.

282
13:59.486 --> 14:00.320
Of course.

283
14:05.325 --> 14:06.368
Let's lock eyes.

284
14:08.703 --> 14:10.163
Can you hold it for four seconds?

285
14:10.288 --> 14:14.167
If I hold it for a long time, You gotta grant me one wish.

286
14:17.962 --> 14:18.797
Deal.

287
14:25.053 --> 14:26.304
[light music playing]

288
14:32.644 --> 14:33.478
[gasps]

289
14:34.979 --> 14:36.773
What? It was a trap!

290
14:38.817 --> 14:41.653
-That's cheating! -It's not cheating. We have no rules.

291
14:44.948 --> 14:46.408
You have to keep your promise.

292
14:46.991 --> 14:48.326
I held it for a long time.

293
14:48.451 --> 14:51.037
I'm never telling you what you want to know, Su-a.

294
14:52.205 --> 14:53.289
Don't expect it.

295
14:53.540 --> 14:55.667
I can figure it out on my own.

296
14:55.792 --> 14:57.252
I'm kind of good at that.

297
15:00.046 --> 15:01.715
If I hold it for a long time…

298
15:03.800 --> 15:05.593
tell me a secret that Mi-do doesn't know.

299
15:06.052 --> 15:07.095
I want to know.

300
15:08.972 --> 15:10.348
[music rises]

301
15:15.145 --> 15:16.229
All right.

302
15:17.313 --> 15:18.148
You better.

303
15:22.777 --> 15:23.695
I will do it one day.

304
15:23.820 --> 15:24.863
I promise I will.

305
15:25.363 --> 15:26.489
Your traps no longer work.

306
15:33.580 --> 15:34.706
[chuckles]

307
15:36.416 --> 15:37.459
[light music concludes]

308
15:45.717 --> 15:46.843
[Mun-yeong] That's not it.

309
15:47.635 --> 15:48.678
You let me go.

310
15:49.512 --> 15:52.182
And back then, I really loved you.

311
15:53.349 --> 15:55.143
Mun-yeong! Mun-yeong!

312
15:55.268 --> 15:56.936
-Hey, what are you doing? -[downbeat music playing]

313
15:57.061 --> 15:58.480
I get it, I messed up, huh?

314
15:58.605 --> 15:59.898
I can't live without you!

315
16:00.023 --> 16:01.149
Don't go, Mun-yeong!

316
16:01.691 --> 16:03.276
I'm telling you that I'm sorry!

317
16:03.401 --> 16:04.235
Mun-yeong!

318
16:05.111 --> 16:06.196
Mun-yeong!

319
16:06.905 --> 16:09.282
Even if you hate me, please open the door!

320
16:10.200 --> 16:12.494
I'm really sorry, Mun-yeong!

321
16:13.536 --> 16:16.206
I can't live without you, Mun-yeong!

322
16:16.706 --> 16:17.540
Mun-yeong!

323
16:17.665 --> 16:20.752
SEOUL FAMILY COURT ADMIN COURT

324
16:20.877 --> 16:22.295
[Yeong-do] Please reconsider this.

325
16:22.921 --> 16:24.005
Just give me one more chance.

326
16:24.422 --> 16:26.257
Just one. Just one more chance.

327
16:26.925 --> 16:27.759
Why on earth…

328
16:29.302 --> 16:30.929
Why can't we just be together?

329
16:31.304 --> 16:32.180
Huh?

330
16:33.223 --> 16:34.265
Think about it.

331
16:34.390 --> 16:35.391
I'm begging you.

332
16:35.517 --> 16:36.392
Please.

333
16:56.454 --> 16:57.956
KO MUN-YEONG LAB

334
17:05.630 --> 17:07.173
[music rises]

335
17:10.260 --> 17:12.303
[Yeong-do] I just can't understand why you…

336
17:18.476 --> 17:19.978
[downbeat music concludes]

337
17:24.399 --> 17:25.567
[man sighs]

338
17:33.491 --> 17:36.160
[panting]

339
17:36.286 --> 17:37.912
I can't. I can't go on.

340
17:38.037 --> 17:39.038
I'm too tired.

341
17:39.163 --> 17:41.749
[panting]

342
17:41.875 --> 17:43.459
You used to be an excellent runner.

343
17:43.835 --> 17:45.461
-Just run. -Hey, hey, hey, hey.

344
17:45.962 --> 17:47.505
I'm in my thirties now, huh?

345
17:47.630 --> 17:50.675
And lately, do-re-mi-fa Sol is driving me nuts.

346
17:51.384 --> 17:53.761
And Mi-do, she's been MIA for days.

347
17:53.887 --> 17:55.013
[sighs]

348
17:55.138 --> 17:56.097
[sighs]

349
17:56.222 --> 17:59.017
At times like this, I guess I'm just like her.

350
17:59.142 --> 18:00.977
[panting]

351
18:01.102 --> 18:01.936
[Wan-do] I'm sad.

352
18:04.647 --> 18:05.857
She's been MIA?

353
18:06.274 --> 18:07.317
[Wan-do] Mm-hmm.

354
18:07.442 --> 18:08.568
She said she's sick.

355
18:09.193 --> 18:10.904
You know her pattern when she hides away.

356
18:11.613 --> 18:15.658
Her phone is on and she answers, but she won't show her face.

357
18:16.200 --> 18:17.785
-[sighs] -[Wan-do] What?

358
18:20.038 --> 18:20.872
You didn't know?

359
18:22.332 --> 18:23.458
So what she's been MIA?

360
18:23.875 --> 18:25.001
Just be nice to your sister.

361
18:25.710 --> 18:26.669
Well, she's just…

362
18:30.214 --> 18:31.049
It's been days.

363
18:31.841 --> 18:32.759
Hey, wait!

364
18:34.052 --> 18:35.803
[phone vibrating]

365
18:48.900 --> 18:52.070
TIN CAN BASTARD

366
18:54.155 --> 18:55.531
[exhales deeply]

367
18:56.741 --> 18:59.953
How can you love the man who caused your father's passing?

368
19:01.746 --> 19:02.747
[sighs]

369
19:09.462 --> 19:10.380
[Tae-seung sighs]

370
19:11.339 --> 19:12.340
This is unbelievable.

371
19:12.966 --> 19:14.592
She said she goes to work every weekday.

372
19:14.717 --> 19:15.677
Where is she?

373
19:16.219 --> 19:17.220
[sighs]

374
19:17.971 --> 19:19.555
Does she actually use her phone?

375
19:20.640 --> 19:21.933
[huffs] Jeez.

376
19:22.892 --> 19:23.726
[Wan-do] Oh.

377
19:25.353 --> 19:27.313
That's your army buddy.

378
19:31.067 --> 19:33.987
The lawyer who got into a car accident with Mi-do?

379
19:35.530 --> 19:36.364
So, uh…

380
19:36.990 --> 19:37.949
Gwan-u, idiot!

381
19:39.450 --> 19:40.994
I told you to never come back.

382
19:42.996 --> 19:44.539
[quirky music playing]

383
19:47.834 --> 19:50.461
He lost his home and real estate to crypto.

384
19:50.586 --> 19:52.088
He keeps coming to me for money.

385
19:52.213 --> 19:53.047
I'm going crazy.

386
19:53.172 --> 19:54.257
[scoffs]

387
19:56.676 --> 19:58.428
[laughs]

388
20:14.027 --> 20:15.069
Hey.

389
20:20.408 --> 20:21.367
Sir.

390
20:23.661 --> 20:25.997
Lost it all to crypto, but I can afford this.

391
20:26.497 --> 20:28.416
Yes, sir, I can afford this.

392
20:28.541 --> 20:30.126
No Eggs Royale, my baby's favorite?

393
20:31.878 --> 20:35.381
My baby loves avocado and smoked salmon and Eggs Benedict as well.

394
20:35.506 --> 20:36.340
Remember.

395
20:41.304 --> 20:42.680
[music rises]

396
20:49.937 --> 20:51.355
I'm Daeho Unit, Class Ten.

397
20:51.773 --> 20:52.982
You're from Class Seven.

398
20:53.608 --> 20:55.985
When you were private, your superior, Corporal Puck,

399
20:56.110 --> 20:58.279
was beating the crap out of you in the bathroom.

400
20:58.404 --> 20:59.864
I stepped in and saved you.

401
21:00.698 --> 21:03.284
After that, you followed me every time I went to the PX.

402
21:04.285 --> 21:05.661
Ah, by the way,

403
21:05.787 --> 21:08.498
your nickname means crybaby who needs attention.

404
21:09.415 --> 21:10.708
-[huffs] -[cutlery clatters]

405
21:11.751 --> 21:14.295
Our youngest will be ready in five minutes.

406
21:15.213 --> 21:16.631
Memorize the backstory.

407
21:17.381 --> 21:19.759
Now you think you're their father or something?

408
21:20.635 --> 21:21.969
[quirky music concludes]

409
21:23.888 --> 21:24.847
What?

410
21:26.057 --> 21:28.142
Trying to fill the void of the father you killed?

411
21:29.852 --> 21:30.937
Don't do that to Mi-do.

412
21:33.231 --> 21:35.316
Don't take cheap shots like that.

413
21:36.567 --> 21:37.610
Mi-do hates that.

414
21:37.735 --> 21:40.988
[coughs]

415
21:43.032 --> 21:43.866
You already did?

416
21:44.575 --> 21:45.785
[clears throat]

417
21:48.913 --> 21:50.248
[Namgung] Oh.

418
21:51.499 --> 21:52.750
It was because of you.

419
21:54.043 --> 21:55.002
Mi-do…

420
22:03.511 --> 22:04.637
Gwan-u…

421
22:06.139 --> 22:11.227
if you hurt Mi-do any further, you're a dead man.

422
22:13.271 --> 22:14.605
I will kill you.

423
22:22.572 --> 22:26.450
Daeho Unit, Class Seven, from March to November, 2013.

424
22:26.576 --> 22:28.411
And Daeho Unit is in Changwon.

425
22:31.330 --> 22:32.790
He's sharper than he looks.

426
22:33.082 --> 22:34.167
Don't mess up.

427
22:39.881 --> 22:42.091
Hey, you didn't lend him money, did you?

428
22:43.467 --> 22:45.303
I think he's in a pyramid scheme.

429
22:45.803 --> 22:46.637
Careful.

430
22:47.180 --> 22:48.097
[sighs wearily]

431
22:48.222 --> 22:50.308
[Namgung] Look at his eyes. He's lost it.

432
22:51.434 --> 22:52.768
I ordered some food for you.

433
22:52.894 --> 22:54.061
Oh, thanks.

434
22:55.313 --> 22:56.439
[chuckles]

435
22:58.065 --> 22:59.358
[exhales tensely]

436
23:00.693 --> 23:01.944
[Namgung] Let's keep our energy up.

437
23:02.069 --> 23:03.154
Remember to refuel.

438
23:04.488 --> 23:05.323
Ms. Ma?

439
23:05.448 --> 23:06.449
[Ms. Ma] Yes?

440
23:06.574 --> 23:07.658
Oh, thank you.

441
23:09.368 --> 23:10.411
Here.

442
23:16.876 --> 23:18.002
Change my name.

443
23:18.419 --> 23:19.253
No way.

444
23:19.670 --> 23:20.713
Hey!

445
23:22.089 --> 23:25.760
Dad, I was too scared to ask you this before.

446
23:27.053 --> 23:30.973
Listen, my name, Sang-su, means value that never changes.

447
23:32.308 --> 23:34.018
Did you name me that to signify

448
23:34.143 --> 23:36.979
your never-changing and eternal marriage?

449
23:37.104 --> 23:38.105
That is right.

450
23:40.358 --> 23:42.026
I tried to tell them it was a bad idea.

451
23:43.569 --> 23:45.154
[quirky music playing]

452
23:45.613 --> 23:47.281
Yeah! I knew it.

453
23:47.406 --> 23:49.408
I was sure. That's why I didn't ask.

454
23:49.533 --> 23:51.827
Just let me change my name already.

455
23:51.953 --> 23:54.288
Hey, stop it. Are you really going to be like this?

456
23:56.082 --> 23:57.083
Oh, no.

457
23:57.625 --> 24:00.378
Change my name. Oh, please.

458
24:00.503 --> 24:01.629
Na-ri Na-ri Pak Na-ri

459
24:03.381 --> 24:05.925
The girl from the Hanbok shop was named Pak Na-ri, right?

460
24:09.762 --> 24:11.097
The lettuce is dirty.

461
24:11.555 --> 24:12.848
I'll go wash it.

462
24:16.477 --> 24:17.645
Who's Nari?

463
24:18.312 --> 24:19.772
[quirky music concludes]

464
24:22.817 --> 24:24.694
I'm the tallest in my whole class.

465
24:25.861 --> 24:27.405
You take after Namgung, huh?

466
24:27.905 --> 24:28.948
He was the tallest.

467
24:29.073 --> 24:30.825
I'm gonna be taller than him.

468
24:32.326 --> 24:33.619
[Sang-su groans]

469
24:33.744 --> 24:35.579
There are mosquitoes everywhere.

470
24:36.247 --> 24:37.748
I'm not eating. I don't want it.

471
24:37.873 --> 24:39.208
Nari Nari Gaenari

472
24:43.254 --> 24:44.088
Ah!

473
24:44.505 --> 24:45.339
Oh, good boy.

474
24:45.756 --> 24:46.674
You look like Karina.

475
24:47.216 --> 24:48.092
[Yeong-do chuckles]

476
24:48.217 --> 24:49.385
Just like Namgung, huh?

477
24:50.011 --> 24:51.679
Come on. He just has a good eye.

478
24:52.388 --> 24:55.641
Grandma, can I come over whenever I want more japchae?

479
24:55.766 --> 24:56.600
Sure.

480
24:57.143 --> 24:59.562
You can come over whenever you want. [chuckles]

481
24:59.687 --> 25:00.980
No.

482
25:02.273 --> 25:03.774
You're going to the shelter tomorrow.

483
25:04.275 --> 25:05.568
That's why we all came here.

484
25:07.862 --> 25:09.947
You're not going to see these people again.

485
25:11.365 --> 25:12.533
It's the last time.

486
25:14.994 --> 25:16.579
[sorrowful music playing]

487
25:21.625 --> 25:22.585
BROTHER CLEANING

488
25:22.710 --> 25:25.296
Hey, man, did you have to go that far?

489
25:27.882 --> 25:28.883
Why is it the last time?

490
25:29.550 --> 25:32.386
-If he's at Pastor Kim's, maybe-- -I'll seek adoption abroad.

491
25:34.347 --> 25:36.682
If Hwa-young and Ju-wan waive custody,

492
25:37.433 --> 25:39.477
I'll be appointed as his legal guardian.

493
25:40.436 --> 25:41.854
Then I'll send him abroad.

494
25:42.688 --> 25:43.564
Hey, Namgung--

495
25:43.689 --> 25:47.234
In Korea nowadays, you can't hide blood ties.

496
25:48.402 --> 25:50.196
Not even through legal means.

497
25:50.905 --> 25:52.656
A PI can uncover anything.

498
25:54.283 --> 25:56.327
Mi-do is already attached to him.

499
25:59.246 --> 26:00.206
She pities him.

500
26:01.415 --> 26:02.666
She sees me in him.

501
26:03.334 --> 26:04.627
She feels sorry for him.

502
26:04.752 --> 26:06.212
She cares for him out of pity.

503
26:06.629 --> 26:07.463
Oh, come on.

504
26:07.588 --> 26:09.173
Are you crazy? It's not like that, you know?

505
26:09.298 --> 26:10.674
You know it, too

506
26:12.009 --> 26:14.220
Mi-do says she pities me a lot.

507
26:17.473 --> 26:18.641
Mi-do doesn't realize it.

508
26:21.602 --> 26:23.354
Plus, she means no harm.

509
26:25.731 --> 26:27.274
However, when she says that,

510
26:28.984 --> 26:30.903
I feel so damn miserable and pathetic.

511
26:32.947 --> 26:34.407
I feel like I'm still seven years old.

512
26:44.917 --> 26:45.751
Sorry.

513
26:47.461 --> 26:48.462
He just made me…

514
26:49.839 --> 26:50.881
[sorrowful music fades]

515
26:51.549 --> 26:52.675
What were you saying?

516
26:53.759 --> 26:55.136
Do I say those things to you?

517
26:56.220 --> 26:58.514
-Mi-do… -I don't say that, Namgung.

518
26:59.723 --> 27:00.891
Am I crazy?

519
27:01.600 --> 27:02.435
Don't lie to me.

520
27:04.186 --> 27:05.896
Actually, you do it often.

521
27:06.021 --> 27:06.981
[Namgung] Hey!

522
27:09.942 --> 27:11.026
You do it often.

523
27:11.902 --> 27:13.487
You do it all the time around us.

524
27:18.576 --> 27:19.743
[exhales sharply]

525
27:23.122 --> 27:24.957
[footsteps approaching rapidly]

526
27:25.875 --> 27:27.001
Hold on a sec.

527
27:27.126 --> 27:28.002
He's exaggerating.

528
27:28.127 --> 27:29.503
Why didn't you tell me before?

529
27:30.546 --> 27:31.839
You should've talked to me.

530
27:32.465 --> 27:35.092
I knew it wasn't ill-intentioned, so it's okay, I swear.

531
27:35.217 --> 27:37.136
How can you be fine with that? Huh?

532
27:37.595 --> 27:38.429
Tell me how!

533
27:41.765 --> 27:43.225
[tender music playing]

534
27:45.519 --> 27:49.231
Namgung, I never thought of you like that.

535
27:49.773 --> 27:50.816
I mean it.

536
27:51.233 --> 27:52.067
Really.

537
27:52.318 --> 27:53.486
I know, Mi-do.

538
27:55.112 --> 27:57.114
You know I always speak without thinking.

539
27:57.865 --> 27:59.366
You know I have no filter,

540
27:59.950 --> 28:02.453
so I just said it without pausing to think.

541
28:03.287 --> 28:05.456
I swear I didn't mean it like that.

542
28:06.165 --> 28:07.374
You're right, Mi-do.

543
28:08.417 --> 28:09.251
Stop it.

544
28:11.253 --> 28:12.087
Namgung,

545
28:13.589 --> 28:16.050
I just wanted to give you everything, you know?

546
28:17.051 --> 28:20.846
I just wanted to give you everything I had in me.

547
28:22.139 --> 28:23.182
I know.

548
28:24.391 --> 28:25.434
I thank you.

549
28:27.603 --> 28:30.064
When you thank me in that kind of way, I just…

550
28:31.482 --> 28:32.525
I feel like…

551
28:40.449 --> 28:41.951
Namgung, I'm sorry.

552
28:43.869 --> 28:45.079
I'm very sorry.

553
28:46.413 --> 28:47.248
I am.

554
28:59.885 --> 29:00.970
What do you mean she quit?

555
29:01.095 --> 29:01.971
[team leader] Yeah.

556
29:02.346 --> 29:04.974
We went out of our way to hire an inexperienced person,

557
29:05.558 --> 29:07.268
and she's been a no-show for three days.

558
29:07.393 --> 29:09.270
[groans] This is ridiculous.

559
29:12.189 --> 29:15.234
PLEASE ANSWER

560
29:18.821 --> 29:20.114
[Namgung] It was because of you.

561
29:20.614 --> 29:25.286
If you hurt Mi-do any further, you're a dead man.

562
29:26.495 --> 29:29.665
[Tae-seung] How can you love the man who caused your father's death?

563
29:32.918 --> 29:34.461
[sighs deeply]

564
29:39.425 --> 29:40.426
[tender music concludes]

565
29:41.135 --> 29:42.803
Sol has grown so much, right?

566
29:42.928 --> 29:43.762
He really has.

567
29:43.887 --> 29:45.431
Sol dear, do you remember the pastor?

568
29:46.056 --> 29:46.932
I don't.

569
29:47.057 --> 29:48.225
[social worker] You really don't?

570
29:48.350 --> 29:49.268
-[laughs] -Say hi.

571
29:49.768 --> 29:50.603
Hello, sir.

572
29:50.728 --> 29:51.562
[social worker] Yes, hello.

573
29:51.687 --> 29:52.813
[Pastor Kim] What a good boy!

574
29:52.938 --> 29:54.815
Shall we go inside? Let's talk.

575
29:54.940 --> 29:56.692
They have a lot of experience.

576
29:56.817 --> 29:58.110
We're gonna do the best we can.

577
29:58.235 --> 29:59.361
[Pastor Kim] He's grown up so well.

578
29:59.486 --> 30:01.280
[social worker] Right? He's grown so much.

579
30:01.530 --> 30:04.575
ANON TEMPORARY CHILD SHELTER

580
30:06.452 --> 30:07.578
[Sol] Namgung!

581
30:20.257 --> 30:21.508
Promise I don't hate you.

582
30:23.135 --> 30:24.053
Don't go away.

583
30:25.763 --> 30:27.056
[sobbing] Please don't go.

584
30:28.599 --> 30:29.892
Don't go away.

585
30:58.295 --> 31:00.339
[gentle, morose music playing]

586
31:04.385 --> 31:05.427
You take care.

587
31:06.762 --> 31:07.596
Sol.

588
31:11.058 --> 31:12.267
Namgung!

589
31:13.352 --> 31:14.186
Namgung!

590
31:14.311 --> 31:16.271
[sobbing]

591
31:16.397 --> 31:18.941
Namgung!

592
31:34.707 --> 31:35.833
Is it…

593
31:37.292 --> 31:38.419
because of me?

594
31:39.837 --> 31:42.631
Pushing him away like that, not getting attached to him?

595
31:43.340 --> 31:44.174
Is it me?

596
31:46.176 --> 31:48.804
If you treat Sol like your mother treated you,

597
31:48.929 --> 31:50.639
we'll all suffer a lot, and so--

598
31:50.764 --> 31:51.807
Just stop.

599
31:54.893 --> 31:56.562
I absolutely hate him.

600
32:00.399 --> 32:01.692
He's just like Han Ju-wan.

601
32:05.237 --> 32:07.281
Looking at him reminds me of Han Ju-wan.

602
32:11.201 --> 32:12.453
Don't you remember…

603
32:13.912 --> 32:14.747
getting attached?

604
32:16.874 --> 32:18.000
It's not the first…

605
32:20.419 --> 32:21.712
time I abandoned him.

606
32:21.837 --> 32:23.172
[gentle, morose music concludes]

607
32:23.881 --> 32:24.882
Is she here?

608
32:25.924 --> 32:27.217
[door bell tinkles]

609
32:27.342 --> 32:28.844
[despondent music playing]

610
32:29.928 --> 32:31.722
[Namgung panting]

611
32:35.392 --> 32:38.562
[social worker] First, please fill out this abandoned child report,

612
32:38.687 --> 32:42.357
then the child transfer agreement for facility placement,

613
32:42.483 --> 32:45.194
and the form confirming you refuse to support him.

614
32:45.736 --> 32:46.820
Please sign here.

615
32:57.748 --> 32:58.916
[music rises]

616
33:13.722 --> 33:15.974
Mi-do, you are my family.

617
33:16.558 --> 33:17.810
Also Ms. Ma.

618
33:18.852 --> 33:19.853
Yeong-do, too.

619
33:21.688 --> 33:22.523
Wan-do.

620
33:23.816 --> 33:25.025
And Sang-su.

621
33:29.071 --> 33:30.239
And that's all of it.

622
33:39.748 --> 33:41.124
[despondent music concludes]

623
33:46.922 --> 33:48.006
Give it here.

624
33:51.093 --> 33:53.262
Wait, you paid, so I'll carry it.

625
33:53.387 --> 33:55.180
Nonsense. Let's carry it together.

626
33:56.139 --> 33:57.558
[Su-a] Dad, are you crazy?

627
33:58.475 --> 33:59.726
That guy has a wife!

628
34:00.269 --> 34:01.228
3 YEARS AGO

629
34:01.353 --> 34:03.605
[Su-a] Listen, Dad, just live as you used to.

630
34:04.231 --> 34:06.108
Since when are you looking for something serious?

631
34:06.692 --> 34:08.527
You didn't last a year with Su-yeon's dad.

632
34:11.947 --> 34:13.073
I looked into it.

633
34:14.533 --> 34:15.409
Look at it.

634
34:15.909 --> 34:19.204
This guy hasn't divorced his wife, and I bet he doesn't plan to.

635
34:19.329 --> 34:20.706
So he's messing with you?

636
34:20.831 --> 34:22.374
He only wants your money.

637
34:23.876 --> 34:27.129
If you keep seeing him, I'll post it online.

638
34:34.636 --> 34:35.637
Don't you dare.

639
34:37.764 --> 34:38.807
I mean it.

640
34:39.516 --> 34:41.101
You'll regret it if you post it.

641
34:43.312 --> 34:44.897
-Dad, but-- -[Yong-dae] Please just stop!

642
34:47.941 --> 34:48.775
Stop it.

643
34:51.820 --> 34:53.155
[exhales deeply]

644
34:58.493 --> 35:00.245
I don't want to be your father anymore.

645
35:02.831 --> 35:03.790
I mean it.

646
35:05.000 --> 35:06.084
[inhales sharply]

647
35:06.209 --> 35:07.586
[somber music playing]

648
35:15.636 --> 35:16.803
[door opens]

649
35:18.138 --> 35:19.222
[door closes]

650
35:22.476 --> 35:25.395
[sobbing]

651
36:05.560 --> 36:06.812
[somber music concludes]

652
36:10.315 --> 36:13.276
[door keypad beeps]

653
36:14.861 --> 36:16.071
[door opens]

654
36:16.947 --> 36:19.074
[indistinct whispering]

655
36:19.199 --> 36:20.742
[footsteps approaching]

656
36:22.577 --> 36:24.204
[Yeong-do] Hey, don't make any noise.

657
36:26.790 --> 36:27.833
Ah…

658
36:34.214 --> 36:37.009
See, I told you he's a light sleeper and would wake up, Mom.

659
36:37.134 --> 36:38.218
[Ms. Ma] Oh…

660
36:38.343 --> 36:40.721
Mom insisted on making you breakfast.

661
36:40.846 --> 36:42.139
You wouldn't come if I asked.

662
36:42.681 --> 36:43.515
Surprise.

663
36:44.099 --> 36:46.768
Dad, you promised me to go to the internet cafe.

664
36:46.893 --> 36:48.020
[Yeong-do sighs]

665
36:48.145 --> 36:48.979
Told them not to.

666
36:50.313 --> 36:51.148
[Ms. Ma] Come on now.

667
36:52.774 --> 36:53.608
Ow.

668
36:59.364 --> 37:00.198
[Mi-do] Hold on.

669
37:01.658 --> 37:02.659
[Sang-su] Uncle.

670
37:03.368 --> 37:04.202
Here.

671
37:07.539 --> 37:11.418
Sol wanted to get you a nice gift or something,

672
37:12.210 --> 37:14.296
so he asked me what sort of thing you like.

673
37:14.880 --> 37:15.881
So I told him.

674
37:17.049 --> 37:19.092
I think I gave him some pretty good advice.

675
37:20.469 --> 37:21.636
[chuckles lightly]

676
37:23.430 --> 37:24.431
[Mi-do] Come on.

677
37:24.973 --> 37:27.225
Oh, how is it, huh?

678
37:27.350 --> 37:28.602
[gentle music playing]

679
37:29.269 --> 37:30.979
-[Wan-do] Try this, Yeong-do. -[Mi-do] Is it salty?

680
37:31.772 --> 37:32.606
How is it?

681
37:33.273 --> 37:34.983
Oh, why is it salty?

682
37:35.108 --> 37:36.443
-Mom made it. -Did I?

683
37:36.568 --> 37:37.694
[laughs] Here.

684
37:37.819 --> 37:39.279
[Mi-do] Mom, it's fine. Try it.

685
37:39.404 --> 37:40.864
[Yeong-do] She hasn't cooked in a while.

686
37:43.867 --> 37:45.118
I think it's delicious.

687
37:45.243 --> 37:47.120
-[Mi-do] See, it's good. -[Yeong-do] Yeah, it's good.

688
37:47.245 --> 37:48.705
[Wan-do] It's really good.

689
37:56.713 --> 37:57.547
Sol.

690
38:08.475 --> 38:09.810
Grab your jacket.

691
38:23.156 --> 38:24.282
[Sol groans]

692
38:24.407 --> 38:26.118
[gentle music concludes]

693
38:26.243 --> 38:27.244
[Sol] Ow!

694
38:27.994 --> 38:28.995
Ow!

695
38:29.996 --> 38:31.832
[sobbing] Ow!

696
38:37.087 --> 38:38.171
Darn it.

697
38:55.188 --> 38:56.231
Wow!

698
38:57.149 --> 38:58.984
-Wow! -[euphoric music playing]

699
38:59.109 --> 39:00.235
Wow!

700
39:04.030 --> 39:05.157
Whoa!

701
39:08.535 --> 39:10.120
[music swells]

702
39:15.834 --> 39:17.419
[euphoric music fades]

703
39:20.338 --> 39:21.298
[Namgung] Don't touch.

704
39:21.423 --> 39:22.841
[sentimental music playing]

705
39:24.676 --> 39:25.886
You just look at them.

706
39:34.186 --> 39:35.020
Your name.

707
39:38.315 --> 39:39.399
I gave it to you.

708
39:41.526 --> 39:42.527
[Hwa-young] Say, "brother."

709
39:43.320 --> 39:44.404
Brother. [laughs]

710
39:47.032 --> 39:47.991
What are you going to do?

711
39:49.784 --> 39:51.328
I thought he was a big catch.

712
39:51.870 --> 39:54.331
But he was just a complete and total scumbag.

713
39:56.458 --> 39:58.919
I was just blinded by greed and made a very bad choice.

714
40:03.715 --> 40:06.676
And now, I'll tie him down legally.

715
40:07.594 --> 40:09.471
I'll squeeze every last penny out of him.

716
40:09.596 --> 40:11.681
Yes, his mom's side is wealthy.

717
40:11.806 --> 40:13.016
Ugh, Mom!

718
40:19.064 --> 40:19.898
Pick something.

719
40:20.023 --> 40:20.857
Huh?

720
40:24.152 --> 40:25.237
[sighs wearily]

721
40:29.241 --> 40:31.618
BIRTH REGISTRATION FORM

722
40:35.872 --> 40:38.124
[Namgung] It's not Sol from the musical scale.

723
40:39.626 --> 40:41.002
It means pine tree.

724
40:41.127 --> 40:42.045
NAME: HAN SOL

725
40:42.462 --> 40:44.547
I named you that so you'd grow up strong.

726
40:47.050 --> 40:48.093
Do you like it?

727
40:49.678 --> 40:51.596
Well, it's not bad at all.

728
40:55.642 --> 40:56.810
[sentimental music fades]

729
40:56.935 --> 40:57.811
Sol.

730
40:57.936 --> 40:59.020
Huh?

731
41:00.397 --> 41:03.608
A lot of people are going to pity you when you get older.

732
41:04.943 --> 41:08.989
And because they pity you, they're going to love you.

733
41:10.782 --> 41:12.033
[Mi-do] The japchae's good.

734
41:12.450 --> 41:13.493
[Ms. Ma] Want some more?

735
41:13.618 --> 41:14.494
That's good.

736
41:14.619 --> 41:15.745
Me too.

737
41:15.870 --> 41:17.330
[Ms. Ma] Here, try some of this, okay?

738
41:17.455 --> 41:18.873
[sweet Korean ballad playing]

739
41:18.999 --> 41:23.545
[Namgung] There will be times when you feel miserable and pathetic.

740
41:24.963 --> 41:31.011
But Sol, loving someone out of pity is truly a warm feeling.

741
41:32.220 --> 41:33.596
It's not fake, it's real.

742
41:34.639 --> 41:36.308
It's genuine love for you.

743
41:36.558 --> 41:38.143
[Mi-do] Oh, I haven't tasted it yet.

744
41:52.240 --> 41:53.325
Know this.

745
41:55.410 --> 41:57.620
Just because you feel miserable or pathetic…

746
42:00.165 --> 42:03.251
do not doubt that love or push it away, never in your life.

747
42:07.255 --> 42:09.257
You have to know what it's worth

748
42:10.300 --> 42:14.346
and be thankful, learn to love others in return.

749
42:16.681 --> 42:17.891
That's how you live.

750
42:25.774 --> 42:28.902
And above all, even if other people pity you,

751
42:30.195 --> 42:33.823
you must never pity yourself.

752
42:33.948 --> 42:35.367
You have to learn that now.

753
42:38.661 --> 42:43.541
You need to be someone who loves and cherishes yourself the most.

754
42:45.585 --> 42:51.758
Only then can you love others and accept the love they give you.

755
42:52.634 --> 42:55.095
[presenter speaking indistinctly]

756
42:55.220 --> 42:56.221
[Namgung] Listen, Sol,

757
42:57.597 --> 43:01.184
make sure you grow up loving yourself.

758
43:04.187 --> 43:05.855
[sweet Korean ballad concludes]

759
43:07.899 --> 43:11.236
[muffled upbeat music playing over speakers]

760
43:11.361 --> 43:13.947
[panting]

761
43:18.618 --> 43:20.787
[man] This jerk picked a fight with me first.

762
43:21.663 --> 43:26.793
Detective, he's obviously a drug addict or an escapee from a mental ward.

763
43:26.918 --> 43:30.630
I seriously hit my head on the asphalt and-- [groans]

764
43:30.755 --> 43:33.216
Ah! My head hurts.

765
43:34.801 --> 43:36.219
Mr. Han Tae-seung,

766
43:36.344 --> 43:39.013
you were sent home last time for a psychiatric evaluation,

767
43:39.139 --> 43:40.265
but not this time.

768
43:40.890 --> 43:43.184
There were no security cameras, but we have witnesses.

769
43:43.852 --> 43:44.686
Call your guardian.

770
43:45.270 --> 43:46.980
[man] He really is a psycho.

771
43:47.105 --> 43:49.065
Please, sir, lock him up right now!

772
43:49.190 --> 43:51.901
[detective] I understand, so calm down and sit, please.

773
43:52.026 --> 43:52.861
Jeez.

774
43:52.986 --> 43:54.904
[man groans] My head.

775
43:58.950 --> 44:00.076
[Ho-sik] It was you!

776
44:00.201 --> 44:02.203
You requested the company audit in the warehouse.

777
44:04.789 --> 44:06.291
I was just following the manual.

778
44:07.667 --> 44:10.295
Any unauthorized disposal is subject to audit.

779
44:10.712 --> 44:13.214
You know exactly why I tossed it, punk.

780
44:17.051 --> 44:20.388
I understand that you despise all the cheap ingredients that we use,

781
44:21.055 --> 44:23.933
but they're safe and they are approved by the MFDS.

782
44:24.601 --> 44:27.020
You can't just toss them without authorization.

783
44:27.145 --> 44:28.771
-[low, tense music playing] -[grunts]

784
44:28.897 --> 44:30.273
-Whoa, whoa, whoa! -Hey!

785
44:30.398 --> 44:32.525
-Stop it, Manager Eom! -Manager Eom! Just relax.

786
44:32.650 --> 44:33.568
Let go of him.

787
44:34.986 --> 44:36.488
[laughs awkwardly] Yeah, continue.

788
44:37.780 --> 44:38.615
How?

789
44:39.365 --> 44:40.867
How could you do this to me?

790
44:41.326 --> 44:42.243
Huh?

791
44:53.129 --> 44:54.506
[low, tense music concludes]

792
44:55.590 --> 44:58.092
[Sang-hun] The fall launch is definitely dead.

793
44:58.760 --> 45:01.596
And if you get disciplined…

794
45:03.097 --> 45:06.142
He thinks he's the boss and in control, huh?

795
45:07.101 --> 45:09.354
After everything I did for him. [scoffs]

796
45:10.396 --> 45:11.397
Hmm?

797
45:13.358 --> 45:14.442
-Whoa! -[gasps]

798
45:14.567 --> 45:16.361
-I'm so sorry. -[Sang-hun] It's fine.

799
45:16.486 --> 45:18.029
I'll go to the restroom. Uh…

800
45:18.863 --> 45:19.864
Continue.

801
45:21.199 --> 45:22.575
[Ho-sik sighs wearily]

802
45:24.536 --> 45:26.996
We've been co-workers for years, huh?

803
45:27.580 --> 45:29.582
And he backstabs me in just three months?

804
45:31.167 --> 45:32.252
It's obvious, sir.

805
45:33.336 --> 45:34.337
Is it?

806
45:35.046 --> 45:36.631
Wait, what is?

807
45:36.756 --> 45:39.092
I know that you and Namgung are staging it.

808
45:39.217 --> 45:40.426
You can stop acting.

809
45:40.969 --> 45:42.178
Why are you saying that?

810
45:42.303 --> 45:43.680
You saw us fighting at the office.

811
45:43.805 --> 45:45.306
I grabbed him and shook him and everything.

812
45:45.431 --> 45:46.849
You'll have a disciplinary hearing,

813
45:47.100 --> 45:49.143
and you also risk a pretty big pay cut.

814
45:49.852 --> 45:51.896
Yet you're buying expensive pork ribs?

815
45:52.021 --> 45:53.439
That doesn't make any sense.

816
45:54.440 --> 45:57.068
Well, times like this call for having lunch with friends.

817
45:57.485 --> 45:59.195
-It makes sense. -Hmm…

818
46:00.196 --> 46:01.823
If that's the case, why did you buy us

819
46:01.948 --> 46:03.825
cheap happy hour specials when the fifth sample

820
46:03.950 --> 46:05.076
fell completely through?

821
46:06.119 --> 46:07.287
Well, that was…

822
46:09.622 --> 46:10.623
[cutlery clatters]

823
46:10.748 --> 46:14.377
If you don't tell me your plan right now, I'll tell Mr. Baek everything.

824
46:17.130 --> 46:18.673
Were you always like this, Su-a?

825
46:19.716 --> 46:21.259
Anyway, never mind that.

826
46:22.260 --> 46:23.344
How much do you know?

827
46:25.430 --> 46:26.389
[exhales sharply]

828
46:27.807 --> 46:29.976
[indistinct chatter]

829
46:57.587 --> 46:59.255
Hey, forget what that detective said.

830
46:59.756 --> 47:01.174
I usually black out when I drink.

831
47:01.591 --> 47:02.800
And I drank a lot.

832
47:04.427 --> 47:05.595
I'm telling the truth.

833
47:05.720 --> 47:06.721
You don't buy it?

834
47:06.846 --> 47:08.181
You think this is all an act?

835
47:08.306 --> 47:09.223
Okay, fine.

836
47:09.349 --> 47:10.391
You're right.

837
47:12.644 --> 47:13.686
You ignored all of my calls.

838
47:13.811 --> 47:15.104
What else could I do?

839
47:15.229 --> 47:17.023
I had to get your attention somehow.

840
47:18.066 --> 47:19.150
All this is your fault.

841
47:23.696 --> 47:25.198
Is your rage meter out of level five?

842
47:25.782 --> 47:26.824
Or level six?

843
47:30.370 --> 47:31.663
[sighs]

844
47:31.788 --> 47:32.955
Okay, I'm sorry.

845
47:33.414 --> 47:35.083
I know I crossed the line that day.

846
47:36.376 --> 47:37.460
[Attorney Lee] Attorney Han?

847
47:46.928 --> 47:48.304
Are you here for a case?

848
47:48.971 --> 47:51.391
Oh, I was worried when you left Jaekang.

849
47:51.933 --> 47:53.226
Guess people still hire you.

850
47:53.351 --> 47:55.186
Heard you did well with that Hanbuk case.

851
47:56.062 --> 47:56.896
Congrats.

852
47:57.397 --> 47:59.107
Stop disgracing our profession.

853
48:00.400 --> 48:01.567
[tense music playing]

854
48:01.693 --> 48:05.530
Drinking parties, lobbying, stop surviving on things like that.

855
48:06.656 --> 48:08.991
Honestly, I'm ashamed to be a lawyer,

856
48:09.117 --> 48:10.618
and it's because of people like you.

857
48:14.080 --> 48:15.039
Ashamed?

858
48:17.750 --> 48:18.960
You're ashamed of losing?

859
48:20.461 --> 48:22.422
Unlike you, my parents aren't prosecutors.

860
48:22.797 --> 48:24.674
To win, I have to do whatever it takes.

861
48:30.054 --> 48:31.097
Congrats.

862
48:32.724 --> 48:34.100
You've even killed someone.

863
48:34.767 --> 48:36.352
So acting like a piece of shit must be easy.

864
48:38.020 --> 48:39.063
[music rises]

865
48:40.189 --> 48:42.233
I swear I will sexually harass you in one minute.

866
48:43.901 --> 48:46.195
If you don't leave, I'll pull your pants down

867
48:46.320 --> 48:48.030
right here and I will shame you in front of everyone.

868
48:48.448 --> 48:52.201
I'm strong enough to strip you and leave you with only your underwear.

869
48:53.202 --> 48:54.036
Really.

870
48:54.287 --> 48:55.163
I'll do it.

871
48:55.288 --> 48:57.290
What the hell are you saying?

872
48:57.832 --> 48:58.666
Twenty seconds left.

873
49:00.084 --> 49:01.085
[Attorney Lee] Fuck it.

874
49:01.210 --> 49:02.253
You two are nuts.

875
49:14.599 --> 49:15.558
[tense music concludes]

876
49:15.683 --> 49:16.726
Yeah, let's go!

877
49:16.851 --> 49:17.852
Round four!

878
49:17.977 --> 49:19.061
[laughing]

879
49:19.187 --> 49:20.855
-Round four! [laughs] -Let's go!

880
49:21.522 --> 49:22.482
[Dong-hwan groans]

881
49:23.065 --> 49:24.734
I feel… good!

882
49:24.859 --> 49:25.735
Thank you!

883
49:26.235 --> 49:27.278
See you tomorrow!

884
49:27.403 --> 49:28.863
-[Namgung] See ya! -[Dong-hwan] See ya!

885
49:32.033 --> 49:36.120
Hey, let's have one more drink. Hmm?

886
49:36.245 --> 49:39.707
I have so much I want to talk to you about!

887
49:39.832 --> 49:45.213
Listen, I booked that lounge club you said you wanted to go to.

888
49:45.338 --> 49:46.380
A club?

889
49:46.506 --> 49:47.465
So let's go home.

890
49:47.590 --> 49:48.424
For now.

891
49:48.549 --> 49:49.383
Huh?

892
49:49.842 --> 49:51.135
-Next week. -Next week?

893
49:51.385 --> 49:52.470
Let's go there!

894
49:52.595 --> 49:54.639
Well, let's go next week!

895
49:55.306 --> 49:56.140
[laughs]

896
49:56.682 --> 49:58.184
-[Namgung] In you go. -[Yeon-ho groans]

897
49:59.644 --> 50:00.645
Bye.

898
50:00.770 --> 50:01.604
Let's go.

899
50:02.271 --> 50:03.564
Next week!

900
50:12.990 --> 50:14.492
[sighs deeply]

901
50:46.607 --> 50:48.651
[sentimental music playing]

902
51:09.422 --> 51:10.256
Sol…

903
51:14.677 --> 51:16.053
I really don't hate you.

904
51:20.057 --> 51:21.601
I actually care about you.

905
51:25.479 --> 51:27.565
And way more than I could ever imagine.

906
51:30.568 --> 51:34.405
But dear Sol, I care about myself more.

907
51:36.073 --> 51:39.243
And I promise I'm going to try.

908
51:42.121 --> 51:44.582
I'm going to try loving myself.

909
51:46.834 --> 51:48.294
That's why I won't stay.

910
51:49.378 --> 51:50.963
So I won't feel sorry for you,

911
51:51.964 --> 51:56.260
and I will always love you and care for you a lot.

912
51:58.596 --> 51:59.805
Listen, Sol.

913
52:01.933 --> 52:03.476
[sobbing softly]

914
52:03.601 --> 52:04.894
Could you please…

915
52:07.772 --> 52:11.442
not hate me too much and think fondly of me.

916
52:39.512 --> 52:40.805
[Su-a] Namgung!

917
52:40.930 --> 52:42.723
[sentimental music fades]

918
52:42.848 --> 52:43.683
[Namgung] Hey.

919
52:44.850 --> 52:46.227
It's Park Su-a.

920
52:47.812 --> 52:48.854
Oh, my gosh.

921
52:48.980 --> 52:50.064
How much did you drink?

922
52:52.191 --> 52:53.651
Wait, I'll go buy some water.

923
52:54.402 --> 52:55.236
Su-a…

924
53:01.659 --> 53:02.493
You know,

925
53:03.244 --> 53:04.370
last time…

926
53:06.831 --> 53:08.374
what you told me?

927
53:09.792 --> 53:12.712
When I said my dream was to be a general manager?

928
53:14.130 --> 53:15.965
What you told me at the store.

929
53:17.633 --> 53:18.467
Huh?

930
53:19.260 --> 53:20.678
That I used to be an outcast?

931
53:21.262 --> 53:22.096
No.

932
53:22.680 --> 53:24.348
Oh, that life isn't a K-drama?

933
53:24.473 --> 53:26.434
I said that, not you.

934
53:26.559 --> 53:27.393
Oh.

935
53:29.395 --> 53:30.980
That I'm resilient, that right?

936
53:31.480 --> 53:32.440
No.

937
53:33.691 --> 53:35.484
It's not that.

938
53:40.698 --> 53:42.199
I said your dream is cool.

939
53:43.451 --> 53:44.285
Yeah.

940
53:46.871 --> 53:47.705
That.

941
53:52.126 --> 53:54.211
Can you say it one more time?

942
53:56.088 --> 53:57.757
[sweet music playing]

943
54:04.764 --> 54:05.848
You are cool.

944
54:09.894 --> 54:12.146
You're a very cool person, really.

945
54:27.995 --> 54:28.913
[gasps]

946
54:37.755 --> 54:38.964
What are you doing?

947
54:39.924 --> 54:40.758
I'm…

948
54:41.425 --> 54:42.259
I'm not looking.

949
54:42.384 --> 54:43.219
You can cry.

950
54:45.346 --> 54:48.599
Isn't the girlfriend supposed to wipe my tears right now?

951
54:50.101 --> 54:51.560
Then you won't be able to cry.

952
54:52.645 --> 54:53.604
[scoffs]

953
54:57.191 --> 54:58.651
Then just leave.

954
54:59.693 --> 55:00.528
No.

955
55:01.362 --> 55:02.446
I'll stay with you.

956
55:03.989 --> 55:04.824
So…

957
55:05.866 --> 55:06.742
just tell me

958
55:07.535 --> 55:08.786
when you're done crying.

959
55:08.911 --> 55:09.745
[clears throat]

960
55:10.538 --> 55:12.039
[chuckles]

961
55:16.752 --> 55:19.922
[crying softly]

962
55:28.764 --> 55:29.849
[sniffs]

963
55:33.060 --> 55:34.687
[chuckles]

964
55:39.567 --> 55:40.734
You're so silly.

965
55:42.570 --> 55:44.321
[sobbing]

966
55:56.417 --> 55:58.085
[sweet music concludes]

967
56:05.217 --> 56:06.677
It was wrong for me to say that.

968
56:10.598 --> 56:11.557
It was wrong.

969
56:13.392 --> 56:14.226
And I'm really sorry.

970
56:16.604 --> 56:20.149
It's just that I really care about you…

971
56:22.651 --> 56:24.153
and wanted what you and Namgung had.

972
56:31.827 --> 56:33.287
Are you just gonna stand there?

973
56:42.504 --> 56:43.631
[exhales softly]

974
56:46.800 --> 56:47.801
Hey, Mi-do.

975
56:50.721 --> 56:52.473
Is this where you and I end?

976
57:06.612 --> 57:08.155
I cannot leave Namgung.

977
57:12.993 --> 57:13.827
You know…

978
57:16.872 --> 57:17.706
that day…

979
57:23.671 --> 57:24.964
Namgung didn't cause…

980
57:29.510 --> 57:30.594
my father's death.

981
57:38.185 --> 57:39.019
I did.

982
57:42.231 --> 57:44.066
[breathes deeply]

983
57:44.942 --> 57:47.027
I'm responsible for his death.

984
57:51.907 --> 57:53.867
-[soft music playing] -[exhales deeply]

985
57:54.785 --> 57:55.911
[man] Someone fell in the water!

986
57:56.036 --> 57:58.163
[woman] Hurry! We need some help!

987
58:03.085 --> 58:04.670
-Papa! -Huh?

988
58:04.795 --> 58:06.338
Hurry up. You have to save him.

989
58:06.463 --> 58:07.298
Please.

990
58:08.340 --> 58:09.174
What are you doing?

991
58:09.300 --> 58:12.303
If something happens to him, I will be very sad.

992
58:13.053 --> 58:15.597
[sobbing] If he dies, it's going to break my heart.

993
58:15.723 --> 58:17.808
Papa, please go right now.

994
58:17.933 --> 58:21.312
You told me need to speak my mind.

995
58:21.437 --> 58:23.439
Dad, hurry and save him now.

996
58:23.564 --> 58:24.523
Go now.

997
58:25.107 --> 58:27.151
Hurry up and save him now.

998
58:27.985 --> 58:29.486
Dad!

999
58:30.154 --> 58:31.155
Daddy!

1000
58:31.280 --> 58:33.157
Oh… [hesitates]

1001
58:33.282 --> 58:34.408
[sobbing]

1002
58:34.658 --> 58:35.659
It's fine.

1003
58:36.243 --> 58:37.244
I'll go save him, okay?

1004
58:40.331 --> 58:41.165
Hurry!

1005
58:41.415 --> 58:42.624
I'll be back!

1006
58:45.294 --> 58:48.964
[young Ms. Ma wailing]

1007
58:52.718 --> 58:53.844
[man] Oh, my God.

1008
58:56.347 --> 58:57.431
It's all your fault.

1009
58:58.766 --> 59:00.768
My husband died because of you.

1010
59:01.352 --> 59:03.520
My kid's dad is dead because of you.

1011
59:04.396 --> 59:06.357
Because of something you did.

1012
59:07.274 --> 59:09.526
He died because of you!

1013
59:10.611 --> 59:13.280
Why did my kid's dad have to die like that?

1014
59:13.947 --> 59:15.240
Why?!

1015
59:16.033 --> 59:19.995
[wailing]

1016
59:26.877 --> 59:30.297
[wailing]

1017
59:37.679 --> 59:38.555
[sniffles]

1018
59:40.474 --> 59:41.600
Namgung doesn't know.

1019
59:42.643 --> 59:43.477
Nobody knows.

1020
59:44.561 --> 59:46.897
I thought everyone would hate me.

1021
59:48.732 --> 59:51.402
I was very afraid and I hid behind him.

1022
59:55.697 --> 59:57.533
I can't leave him ever.

1023
01:00:02.329 --> 01:00:04.081
I have to be there for Namgung.

1024
01:00:06.041 --> 01:00:07.584
[music rises]

1025
01:00:10.379 --> 01:00:11.338
I'm so sorry.

1026
01:00:12.923 --> 01:00:14.508
I was very wrong.

1027
01:00:15.801 --> 01:00:17.094
Apologies won't work.

1028
01:00:19.096 --> 01:00:20.222
I can't be with you.

1029
01:00:21.473 --> 01:00:22.641
That's not it.

1030
01:00:23.600 --> 01:00:24.810
That's not it.

1031
01:00:32.609 --> 01:00:34.445
It must have been so hard.

1032
01:00:37.698 --> 01:00:40.534
[crying] It must have been really hard for you.

1033
01:00:40.659 --> 01:00:41.827
I'm really sorry.

1034
01:00:43.370 --> 01:00:46.790
I… I had no idea.

1035
01:00:49.334 --> 01:00:50.169
I'm sorry.

1036
01:00:50.294 --> 01:00:51.128
Sorry.

1037
01:00:51.420 --> 01:00:52.629
Sorry for saying that.

1038
01:00:52.754 --> 01:00:53.881
[sobs]

1039
01:01:08.562 --> 01:01:10.147
[soft music concludes]

1040
01:01:10.856 --> 01:01:12.024
[groans]

1041
01:01:14.943 --> 01:01:16.445
[grunts]

1042
01:01:19.781 --> 01:01:20.616
[gasps]

1043
01:01:24.328 --> 01:01:25.412
[groans]

1044
01:01:26.872 --> 01:01:28.207
You scared me.

1045
01:01:33.086 --> 01:01:34.254
[grunts softly]

1046
01:01:36.131 --> 01:01:36.965
What's wrong?

1047
01:01:39.343 --> 01:01:40.302
Why do you look…

1048
01:01:46.558 --> 01:01:47.476
Uh…

1049
01:01:56.735 --> 01:01:57.778
[gasps]

1050
01:01:58.278 --> 01:02:00.030
["Stay" playing]

1051
01:02:28.600 --> 01:02:30.477
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

1052
01:02:45.617 --> 01:02:47.619
You wanted to get hurt, like that?

1053
01:02:48.745 --> 01:02:51.123
[Mi-do] Su-a, you like her, right?

1054
01:02:51.748 --> 01:02:53.333
[Su-a] You live like this for Ms. Lee.

1055
01:02:53.458 --> 01:02:54.376
It's for her, right?

1056
01:02:54.501 --> 01:02:55.335
Yeah.

1057
01:02:55.460 --> 01:02:56.878
To me, Mi-do is everything.

1058
01:02:57.004 --> 01:02:58.088
Are you disappointed?

1059
01:02:58.213 --> 01:02:59.339
[Tae-seung] Oh, no.

1060
01:03:00.048 --> 01:03:01.383
I think I really like you.

1061
01:03:01.842 --> 01:03:03.343
We break up in about ten days.

1062
01:03:03.677 --> 01:03:04.761
Will you sleep with me?

1063
01:03:05.304 --> 01:03:06.471
[Mi-do] Stop liking her.

1064
01:03:07.764 --> 01:03:08.724
Stop liking her.

1065
01:03:09.850 --> 01:03:10.767
Stop.

1066
01:03:15.063 --> 01:03:16.023
[song concludes]
